  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Feasibility Study - PORT OF BUENAVENTURA OPERATIONAL AND SECURITY ENHANCEMENT PROJECT, through Government of Colombia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This $400,000 operational and security enhancement feasibility study for the Sociedad Portuaria Regional de Buenaventura evaluates existing conditions, procedures and equipment, determines and recommends improvements, prepares technical background material, and addresses the implementation of a container scanning facility at the Port of Buenaventura on Colombia&apos;s Pacific Coast. The port is a multipurpose facility handling containers, bulk cargo, break cargo, vehicles, and general cargo. Colombian governmental agencies such as the Tax and Customs Administration and the Office of the Superintendent of Ports and Transport have made security at all major ports a priority.</narrative>
  </description>
